otic acid to fluorodeoxyuridine, which is toxic to cells.\nL49: Stars  【75†Image】【76†Image】【77†Image】 This entity has been manually annotated by the ChEBI Team.\nL50: Roles Classification\nL51: 【28†Chemical Role】(s): 【29†Bronsted acid】\nL52: A molecular entity capable of donating a hydron to an acceptor (Br o nsted base).\nL53: \nL54: (via 【30†oxoacid】 )\nL55: \nL56: 【31†View more via ChEBI Ontology】    ChEBI Ontology\nL57: Outgoing  5-fluoroorotic acid (【32†CHEBI:74498】)  is a  nucleobase analogue (【33†CHEBI:67142】)\nL58: 5-fluoroorotic acid (【32†CHEBI:74498】)  is a  organofluorine compound (【34†CHEBI:37143】)\nL59: 5-fluoroorotic acid (【32†CHEBI:74498】)  is a  pyrimidinemonocarboxylic acid (【35†CHEBI:26447】)\nL60: IUPAC Name\nL61: 5-fluoro-2,6-dioxo-1,2,3,6-tetrahydropyrimidine-4-carboxylic acid\nL62: Synonyms  Sources\nL63: 1,2,3,6-tetrahydro-2,6-dioxo-5-fluoro-4-pyrimidinecarboxylic acid  ChemIDplus 【78†Image: Indicates when synonyms have been adapted from the specified source i.e. not exact copies.】\nL64: 5-fluoro-1,2,3,6-tetrahydro-2,6-dioxo-4-pyrimidinecarboxylic acid  ChEBI\nL65: 5-fluoro-6-carboxyuracil  ChEBI\nL66: 5-fluorouracil-4-carboxylic acid  ChemIDplus 【79†Image: Indicates when synonyms have been adapted from the specified source i.e. not exact copies.】\nL67: ENT-26398  ChemIDplus\nL68: FO  ChemIDplus\nL69: FOA  ChemIDplus\nL70: NSC 31712  ChemIDplus\nL71: NSC-31712  ChEBI\nL72: Ro 2-9945  ChemIDplus\nL73: Manual Xrefs  Databases\nL74: 【36†GB806584†worldwide.espacenet.com】  Patent\nL75: 【37†US2948725†worldwide.espacenet.com】  Patent\nL76: 【38†View more database links】\nL77: \nL78: Registry Numbers  Types  Sources\nL79: 181933  Reaxys Registry Number  Reaxys\nL80: 【39†703-95-7†chem.nlm.nih.gov】  CAS Registry Number  ChemIDplus\nL81: \nL82:   Citations  【80†Image: Waiting for Citations】  Types  Sources\nL83:   2675756  PubMed citation  Europe PMC\nL84: 3323810  PubMed citation  Europe PMC\nL85: 3586772  PubMed citation  Europe PMC\nL86: Last Modified 【